UID:qf6rhs7dag6ctcg3ppg7uvek60@google.com
CREATED:20260805T041650Z
DESCRIPTION:Alma Sangre and The Latin Jazz Trio together at The Actors Stud
 io!\n \nTHE LATIN JAZZ TRIO is composed of John Tavano (classical guitar)\,
  Roger Kimball (bass & cello)\, and Cinnamon Blomquist (flute).\n \nALMA SA
 NGRE is a borderless duo moving between Los Angeles and Mexico\, crafting a
  sound rooted in tradition but untethered to any single genre. Their music 
 draws from the trance-like grooves of Ali Farka Touré\, the raw emotional g
 ravity of Chavela Vargas\, and the rhythmic pulse of Latin and Afro-Caribbe
 an forms—filtered through a distinctly modern\, cinematic lens.\nAt the cor
 e of Alma Sangre are singer/guitarist Antonio Aguilar (featured in Premier 
 Guitar Magazine) and multi-instrumentalist and dancer Meg Castellanos. Thei
 r performances blur the line between concert and ritual—melding intricate g
 uitar work\, Spanish-language lyricism\, and expressive movement into somet
 hing immersive and transportive.\n \nAlma Sangre creates music that feels b
 oth ancient and immediate—made for listeners drawn to global sounds\, emoti
 onal depth\, and performances that resonate long after the final note.\n \n
 Ay mi Dios official music video\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hjxoDeWGxA
 k&list=RDhjxoDeWGxAk&start_radio=1\n \n \nWhen: : Saturday August 22\, 2026
   7:30 PM\nWhere: 1 Merrill Street\, Cross Roads Plaza – Salisbury\, MA\nTi
 ckets:   $25\n \n \nBuy tickets here\n \n \nThe Actors Studio was founded i
 n 1991 and  is a 501C(3) 65 seated theater which is a vital cultural resour
 ce for the community: to inspire\, enrich and engage audiences and to devel
 op both the art form and the individual by encouraging full creative expres
 sion.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260805T041652Z
LOCATION:The Actors Studio – Crossroads Plaza\, 1 Merrill Street\, Unit # 3
 \, Salisbury\, MA\, 01952
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:​[The Actor's Studio of Newburyport\, Newburyport] Alma Sangre with
  the Latin Jazz Trio
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
