UID:4rt86em75ckkhnrcdl4jjukr90@google.com
CREATED:20260805T041650Z
DESCRIPTION:Come and enjoy the music of Larin America and Spain with this w
 onderful trio.\n\n \nAlan Whitney – Jazz Guitar – has been a musician\, edu
 cator and mentor for over four decades. Growing up in the town of Tewksbury
 \, Massachusetts\, Alan started his teaching career at the young age of fou
 rteen. Alan continues to work on multiple projects with numerous trio/ quar
 tet configurations. Alan has been a New England jazz guitar staple\, educat
 or and local favorite for decades and who is known for blending superb tech
 nique with thoughtful interpretation.\n \nRoger Kimball – Bass\, Cello – ha
 s always been interested in diverse musical styles. (Even as a teenager he 
 toured Europe and the Middle East as a cellist with a symphony orchestra an
 d played bass guitar in a rock band.)  Roger has had the honor of playing j
 azz upright bass at New York City’s Bluenote and Shenandoah Jazz festival i
 n Virginia\, among other venues\, and has collaborated with Carlos Santana 
 as well as the late Brad Delp of the band Boston. He regularly teaches cell
 o\, electric bass and upright bass at The Real School of Music in Andover.\
 n \nJohn Tavano – Classical Guitar – has performed repertoire throughout Ne
 w England and Europe ranging from guitar music of the Renaissance and Baroq
 ue period to Flamenco and Jazz. His original compositions and recordings “L
 a Gitana” and “Avila” are currently heard on local radio stations. As a pla
 ywright \,Tavano wrote the play and composed the music  for Fuente Grande\,
  telling the story of the last days of the Spanish poet Federico Garcia Lor
 ca” produced by the Actors Studio of Newburyport and performed at the Fireh
 ouse Center of the Performing Arts. John is currently employed for the Zach
  Field Drum and Music Studio\n \n \nWhen: : Thursday August 6\, 2026  7:00 
 PM\nWhere: 1 Merrill Street\, Cross Roads Plaza – Salisbury\, MA\nTickets: 
   $25\n \n \nBuy tickets here\n \n \nThe Actors Studio was founded in 1991 
 and  is a 501C(3) 65 seated theater which is a vital cultural resource for 
 the community: to inspire\, enrich and engage audiences and to develop both
  the art form and the individual by encouraging full creative expression.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260805T041652Z
LOCATION:The Actors Studio – Crossroads Plaza\, 1 Merrill Street\, Unit # 3
 \, Salisbury\, MA\, 01952
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:​[The Actor's Studio of Newburyport\, Newburyport] Bossa Jazz Trio
TRANSP:OPAQUE
